+---
+id: task-001-add-rental-module-createrentalservice-with-addequipment-quote-book
+type: task
+title: "Add rental module: createRentalService with addEquipment, quote, book"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Export `createRentalService()` from `src/index.ts`: an in-memory rental service with
+`addEquipment(item)`, `quote(request)` and `book(request)`, following the school's money, time,
+whole-day, overlap and (future) cancellation rules. Cancellation itself is out of scope.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Wrote failing tests first in `test/rental-service.test.ts` (red), covering: a happy-path quote and
+  its total; unknown-item errors for `quote` and `book`; periods that don't start/end at midnight UTC;
+  a period shorter than one day; a period that ends before it starts; a happy-path booking with a
+  generated id; overlapping bookings on the same item rejected; adjacent (non-overlapping) bookings on
+  the same item allowed; overlapping bookings allowed across different items.
+- Implemented `src/index.ts` (green): `Equipment`, `RentalRequest`, `Quote`, `Booking` and
+  `RentalService` types, plus `createRentalService()`. Validation (unknown item, non-midnight
+  boundaries, non-positive/invalid period) is shared between `quote` and `book`; `book` additionally
+  checks for an overlapping booking on the same item before recording it. Booking ids are an
+  incrementing per-service sequence (`booking-1`, `booking-2`, ...) to keep the module deterministic —
+  no wall-clock reads, no randomness.
+- All 12 tests pass under `npm test` (`node --test`, using Node 22's native TypeScript support — no
+  build step or added dependency).
+- Documented the module in `README.md` (usage example and the rules it follows).
+- Did not implement cancellation, as requested; the cancellation policy (rule 5) is recorded for later.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `node --test` → 12/12 passing.
